+## D138 — The upscale point at a depth resolve, for a game that never copies its color (2026-11-10)
+
+**Decision:**
+- **`Profile::upscale_resolve_depth`:** with `upscale_resolve_caller`, the copy that ends the main 3D view may resolve the
+  view's *depth* into a color texture. The upscale point then accepts a depth surface of the output size instead of
+  requiring a color one. The view's color stays the target its draws last made (`g_scene_color`); the depth the upscaler
+  reads is the view's own.
+- **GH World Tour's profile sets it.** Its other boundary fields are unchanged: `upscale_resolve_caller =
+  scene_resolve_caller = 0x824AE0D0`, `unscaled_screen_fractions` (D127), no view hooks.
+
+**Why:**
+- **GHWT never copies its 1280x720 color.** A trace dump of a song (`ghworldtour_035`, frame 12000) counts 7 resolves a
+  frame; the frame's 1280x720 color target is resolved only at 640x360 through the 4x MSAA surface the post-processing
+  downsamples with (D95's alias), and the depth is resolved at 1280x720 into `0xABA26C00`
+  (`sub_824ADED0`, return address `0x824AE0D0`) for the depth of field.
+- **Without the flag nothing started.** `upscale_resolve_caller` was set, so `g_auto_views` was on (D119), but the point
+  was guarded by `!surface.depth` and `surface.width == output_width` (D119): every resolve at that caller was the depth
+  one, so the view never ended. `DLAA applied 0 times in 600 frames`, and the camera vote never ran (`0 of 0 views
+  voted`), from boot through the attract mode and into a song. The view did start — the first depth-writing 1280x720 draw
+  with a perspective matrix — so 3D was jittered with no upscale to undo it.
+- **The depth copy is the right boundary anyway.** It is the last thing the view does before the post-processing reads
+  the scene, and the 2D layer (the HUD, the note highway) is drawn after it, so it stays outside the jitter and the
+  temporal history.
+- **The alternative, a color resolve at another caller, does not exist.** Sent to the whole 1280x720 color target there
+  is none; the 640x360 one is a reduced copy (D127 keeps it at its guest size), which the upscaler must not take.
+
+**Evidence** (this machine, RTX 4070 Ti, Vulkan 1.4, `tools/runs/dlaa2`):
+- `DLAA applied 600 times in 600 frames`, camera vote `600 of 600 views voted` (156-277 offers, 151-262 votes for the
+  winner per view) across the attract mode's scenes at 1280x720; the note highway and the HUD keep their 1:1 pixels.
+- The frames before the fix, same command: `0 times in 600 frames`, `0 of 0 views voted`, from frame 1 to the song.
+
+**Limits:**
+- The upscaler runs one call earlier than a color copy would: at the depth resolve, the color target is the view's last
+  drawn target, and the game must not draw into it between that resolve and its own post-processing.
+- A game that resolves depth at several callers, some outside its view, needs one boundary caller that is inside it.
+
+**Revisit if:** GHWT is found to draw into its 1280x720 target after the depth resolve but inside the view (a decal pass,
+a second scene layer), or if another game shows the same "no output-sized color copy" shape.
+## D139 — The 3D view's state in the log, and why an upscale point did not run (2026-11-10)
+
+**Decision:**
+- **One line when the 3D view's state has persisted 30 frames (half a second):** `3D view: none`, `3D view: found, but
+  its upscale point 0x... did not run this frame` (a warning, with the auto views on), `3D view: found (no temporal
+  upscaler)`, or `3D view: upscaled at the profile's point 0x...`. A state that alternates frame to frame writes nothing.
+- **A resolve at the profile's `upscale_resolve_caller` that is not the view's end logs why, once:** no surface, not the
+  output size, or a depth surface with `upscale_resolve_depth` unset (D138).
+- **A warning once, 600 frames after the first 3D view,** when `upscale_resolve_caller` is set and its point has still
+  never run: DLSS or FSR 3.1 cannot start without it.
+
+**Why:**
+- **A silent mismatch looked exactly like "no 3D scene".** GH World Tour logged `DLAA applied 0 times in 600 frames` and
+  `0 of 0 views voted` through the attract mode and a song, while the view was in fact starting (a perspective-matrix
+  draw of the output size) and the resolve at the profile's point was being rejected for being a depth surface. An
+  agent (and a player reading the log) could not tell "the upscaler is off" from "we are in a menu" without patching the
+  library to print the reason.
+- **The check is cheap and bounded:** the state is computed once a frame from two booleans, and a state must hold for
+  30 frames before it is written, so a menu whose view comes and goes writes nothing and a song writes one line.
+- **It names the profile field it is about** (`upscale_resolve_caller`, D119), which is the first thing a new game's
+  porting needs to verify.
+
+**Evidence** (GH World Tour, `tools/runs/dlaa2` and `ghworldtour_058`):
+- Before: no line; `DLAA applied 0 times` with the profile's point set was ambiguous between no view and a rejected
+  point. After D138, `3D view: upscaled at the profile's point 0x824ae0d0` and `DLAA applied 600 times in 600 frames`.
+
+**Limits:**
+- The state is per frame, so a frame that draws 3D but does not reach the point logs `found, but` (a game whose view
+  ends at Present in menu frames will alternate `found, but` and `upscaled`, and the 30-frame rule then writes neither).
+- `3D view: none` includes a frame with a view that never drew (unlikely) and a frame whose view hooks were never
+  called.
+
+**Revisit if:** a 3D view legitimately lasts fewer than 30 frames at a time (a preview thumbnail) and its absence from
+the log misleads.
+
+## D140 — Single-pass motion + depth copy and camera-cut temporal reset in `Upscaler::Apply` (2026-11-14)
+
+**Decision:**
+- **Single-pass motion + depth copy (`motion_depth_pso_`):** When `depth_copy_` is required (FSR 3.1 upscaling or frame
+  generation inputs `frame_inputs_on_`), `Upscaler::Apply` binds both `motion_` (`TEX_FORMAT_RG16_FLOAT`, location 0)
+  and `depth_copy_` (`TEX_FORMAT_R32_FLOAT`, location 1) in a single fullscreen pass (`kMotionAndDepthPS`), eliminating
+  the separate `CopyDepth` fullscreen pass that previously re-read `depth_srv` immediately after `motion_pso_`.
+- **Camera-cut / scene-jump auto-reset:** Before writing reprojection constants in `Upscaler::Apply`, clip-space center
+  `(0, 0, 0.5, 1)` is projected through the active column-major reprojection matrix (`from_vote` or `from_view`). If the
+  reprojected homogeneous `w <= 1e-6`, any component is non-finite, or the single-frame NDC displacement
+  `max(|ndc_x|, |ndc_y|) > 0.75`, `reset = true` is forced so DLAA/DLSS, FSR 3.1, and Frame Generation reset temporal
+  history cleanly instead of ghosting across discontinuous camera cuts.
+
+**Why:**
+- `kMotionPS` already samples `depthTex.Load(int3(sv_pos.xy, 0)).r` and normalizes depth into `[0, 1]` with `0` at the
+  near plane. Writing that normalized depth to `SV_Target1` in the same pass avoids a second fullscreen pass, pipeline
+  switch, and redundant full-resolution depth read every frame when FSR 3.1 or Frame Generation is active.
+- Stage camera cuts in GH World Tour jump instantaneously between viewpoints while keeping a valid invertible
+  view-projection matrix on consecutive frames; without an NDC displacement check, `last_applied_frame_ + 1 == frame_`
+  kept temporal history across the cut and fed full-screen motion vectors into the temporal upscaler and frame generator.
+
+**Limits:**
+- An extremely fast whip-pan exceeding 75% of the screen width/height in a single frame also triggers a 1-frame temporal
+  history reset, which is benign because motion vectors of that magnitude cannot be temporally accumulated cleanly.
+
+**Revisit if:** a game uses an off-center projection where `(0, 0, 0.5, 1)` is outside the view frustum.
+
+## D141 — Stamping `output->written` after reduced-resolution `UpscaleScene` at depth-resolve boundaries (2026-11-14)
+
+**Decision:**
+- In `UpscaleScene` (`renderer.cpp`), when `g_upscaler.Apply` upscales the reduced-resolution 3D scene target
+  (`g_scene_color`, `Kind::kReduced`) into the full render-scale target (`output`, `Kind::kRender`), stamp
+  `output->written = ++g_target_writes;` whenever `upscaled && output != g_scene_color`.
+
+**Why:**
+- With `upscale_resolve_depth = true` (D138), GH World Tour ends its main 3D view at the `0x824AE0D0` depth resolve rather
+  than a full-resolution color resolve, and immediately afterward resolves EDRAM color base `0` through a `640x360` 4x
+  MSAA alias (`RenderTargets::FindMsaaAlias`).
+- `RenderTargets::FindMsaaAlias` and `RenderTargets::Get` select between `Kind::kReduced` and `Kind::kRender` targets at
+  the same EDRAM base by comparing their `written` sequence numbers. Because `UpscaleScene` wrote into `output->texture`
+  via `g_upscaler.Apply` without advancing `output->written`, `g_scene_color->written` (from the last 3D draw) remained
+  newer than `output->written`, causing subsequent post-processing and 2D resolve passes to sample the un-upscaled
+  reduced-resolution `g_scene_color` target instead of the upscaled `Kind::kRender` target in DLSS/FSR Quality,
+  Balanced, and Performance modes.
+
+**Limits:**
+- Applies only when `output != g_scene_color` (upscaling modes where `g_reduced` is active).
+
+**Revisit if:** `UpscaleScene` is ever called on a target that should not become the newest EDRAM base owner.
+
+## D142 — NVIDIA Frame Generation (DLSS-G via NGX Vulkan) with automatic AMD FidelityFX fallback (2026-11-14)
+
+**Decision:**
+- Add `native_x_renderer_frame_generation_provider` (`"auto"` default, `"nvidia"`/`"dlssg"`, `"amd"`/`"fsr3"`).
+- In `device.cpp` (`ProbeVulkanSupport`, under `NATIVE_X_RENDERER_DLSS`), query
+  `NVSDK_NGX_VULKAN_GetFeatureInstanceExtensionRequirements` and
+  `NVSDK_NGX_VULKAN_GetFeatureDeviceExtensionRequirements` for `NVSDK_NGX_Feature_FrameGeneration` and
+  `NVSDK_NGX_Feature_SuperSampling` before creating the DiligentCore Vulkan instance/device, enabling supported
+  extensions and `Features.NativeFence = DEVICE_FEATURE_STATE_OPTIONAL` (`VK_KHR_timeline_semaphore`).
+- In `framegen.{h,cpp}`, add an NVIDIA NGX DLSS-G backend alongside AMD FidelityFX (`amd_fidelityfx_vk.dll`):
+  - Query capability via `NVSDK_NGX_VULKAN_GetCapabilityParameters` (`NVSDK_NGX_Parameter_FrameGeneration_Available`),
+    initializing NGX with `NVSDK_NGX_VULKAN_Init_with_ProjectID` when not already initialized by `DLSSProviderVk`.
+  - Create the DLSS-G feature via `NGX_VK_CREATE_DLSSG` and evaluate via `NGX_VK_EVALUATE_DLSSG` into `output_` using
+    `pBackbuffer` (`current`), `pDepth` (`view.depth`), `pMVecs` (`view.motion` with
+    `mvecScale = {1.0f / motion_width, 1.0f / motion_height}`), `pHudless` (`hudless`), and camera/jitter/subrect
+    parameters.
+  - When `provider == "auto"`, if `FrameGeneration.Available == 0` or `NGX_VK_CREATE_DLSSG` fails on the current
+    GPU/driver/swapchain configuration, log the NGX status code clearly and fall back seamlessly to AMD FidelityFX
+    (`amd_fidelityfx_vk.dll`).
+- In `CMakeLists.txt`, link `DLSS-Headers` and `DLSS-NGX` to `native_x_renderer` when DLSS is enabled and copy
+  `nvngx_dlssg.dll` in `native_x_renderer_copy_runtime` if present alongside `nvngx_dlss.dll`.
+
+**Why:**
+- NVIDIA's `nvsdk_ngx_d.lib` exports the Vulkan NGX entry points (`NVSDK_NGX_VULKAN_*`), and `nvngx_dlssg.dll` is
+  discovered either from the application directory or from the NVIDIA display driver store via NGX's feature discovery.
+- Using `output_` (`pOutputInterpFrame`) with our existing swapchain dual-present path (D123) avoids replacing
+  DiligentCore's Vulkan swapchain while supporting both NVIDIA DLSS-G and AMD FSR 3.1 frame generation under one
+  interface.
+- Seamless fallback in `"auto"` mode ensures non-RTX-40/50 GPUs or environments where NGX disallows standalone Vulkan
+  DLSS-G creation without an interposer continue to get working frame generation via AMD FidelityFX.
+
+**Limits:**
+- Evaluates 2x frame generation (`multiFrameCount = 1`, `multiFrameIndex = 1`), matching the renderer's single
+  interpolated frame presentation before the real frame (D123).
+
+**Revisit if:** multi-frame generation (3x/4x) pacing is added to `ExecutePresent`.
